  "notes": [
    "Next_Posture_risk forecasts the NEXT 1-second window's risk level from the CURRENT window's features; the last window of every (participant, condition, segment) recording has no next window and is dropped.",
    "Evaluation is Leave-One-Participant-Out: every reported metric is on a participant the model never trained on.",
    "'high' (Critical, >45 deg) is rare and concentrated in a few participants -- treat the per-class and per-participant breakdowns as directional, not production-grade precision, and re-evaluate as more participants are collected.",
    "Feedback is NOT fired directly off this model's per-tick output -- see posture_feedback.py: only 3 consecutive 'high' predictions trigger feedback, and any 'low' or 'medium' prediction resets the streak, per the assignment's course-wide requirement."
  ]
